   1294  f278							; --- Clamp fall speed: down at MAX_FALL, up at -$0100. ---
   1295  f278							; The high byte alone is NOT enough (2026-10-22): `cmp #>MAX_FALL` with vyHi
   1296  f278							; == $01 is EQUAL, so the old code rewrote vy to exactly $0180 for every speed
   1297  f278							; in $0100..$017F — a falling player's thrust was computed and then thrown
   1298  f278							; away every frame (vy: $0180 -> $0188 -> $0158 -> clamped back to $0180), so
   1299  f278							; the jet could not slow a fall at all. Compare the low byte when the high
