   2736  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2737  f97a							; E4 moth exit tramp ($FC49-$FC4E) — bank2 executes `sta $1FF6` at $FC49
   2738  f97a							; (byte-identical slice, guard: verify_build), then the fetch at $FC4C comes
   2739  f97a							; from bank0 = `jmp UE_Next` (real label here — no cross-bank address sync).
   2740  f97a							; bank0's `sta $1FF6` copy never runs; bank2's bytes from $FC4C never run.
   2741  f97a							;
   2742  f97a							; MUST stay off $FFF6-$FFF9: those are the ONLY addresses in code space where
   2743  f97a							; (addr & $1FFF) lands in $1FF6-$1FF9 = F6 hotspot mirrors. Stella's
   2744  f97a							; CartridgeEnhanced::peek (CartEnh.cxx:157, ADDR_MASK=$1FFF) calls
   2745  f97a							; checkSwitchBank on READS — the old $FFF2 placement fetched the `jmp`
   2746  f97a							; operands at $FFF6/$FFF7 and flipped banks mid-instruction (operand hi from
   2747  f97a							; bank1 = $00 -> jmp $007D -> HUD runaway, 359/360-line frames, 5-byte stack
   2748  f97a							; leak per rogue Overscan entry -> SP decayed to $E1 -> frame-3 crash where
   2749  f97a							; jsr RefreshEnemyY's return landed on FetchPtr). Real F6 is write-only, but
   2750  f97a							; no fetched byte may ever sit in the mirror zone.
   2751  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2752  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2753  f97a							; Cross-bank call pads (docs/leaf_move_plan.md) — byte-identical copies live in
   2754  f97a							; bank1 at the SAME addresses. F6 hotspots switch on ANY write — the written
   2755  f97a							; value is ignored (proven by FoldIndirect's `sta $1FF6` carrying data bytes) —
   2756  f97a							; so the pads `sta $1FF7`/`sta $1FF6` with A AS-IS: A/X/Y/flags pass through
   2757  f97a							; unchanged, making the pad equivalent to the original inlined `jsr`.
   2758  f97a							; (2026-09-30 bug: `lda #1` before `sta $1FF7` clobbered A — ClearPFColumn
   2759  f97a							; punched col 1 instead of the bomb's col, AddScore added +1 instead of
   2760  f97a							; +50/+75. Hole appeared at screen col 1 + mirror col 18 = "second tile from
   2761  f97a							; each edge"; collision stayed correct because WallMask is separate.)
   2762  f97a							; `sta` does not touch flags — IsRoomDark's `beq` contract survives the
   2763  f97a							; return. Carry survives. No stack use.
   2764  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2765  f97a		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$F9B8 - *, 0	; Phase 4 overlay tramp — shared address with
   2766  f9b8							; bank2's twin image (40B bank2 hole before
   2767  f9b8							; org $F9D9); F6-safe ($F9B1 & $1FFF ∉ hotspots)
   2768  f9b8				   OverlayTramp
   2769  f9b8		       a5 84		      lda	LineCount	; packed asym byte (0 = symmetric)
   2770  f9ba		       f0 03		      beq	.OTsym	; sym: clc/rts, never enters the cluster
   2771  f9bc		       4c 2d fa 	      jmp	PHMOverlay	; bank0 cluster ($FA30; repack chunk 4)
   2772  f9bf				   .OTsym
   2773  f9bf		       18		      clc
   2774  f9c0		       60		      rts
